{% extends "layout.html.twig" %}

{#
  S6 — open opportunities, in the Member Portal (MP6, #9867; Member Portal design
  §5.4, volunteer design §5.6).

  Two lists of the same kind of thing — something a volunteer can say yes to — over
  `GET /api/ministries/me/help-wanted` and `GET /api/ministries/me/opportunities`.
  D19's "Ministries looking for help" comes first with its one **I'd like to help**
  button per ministry; below the section break, "Upcoming availability" holds the
  scheduled positions, each with a single **Sign up** button. The list is server-side
  eligibility, and the server re-validates at signup (§3.3.3, D5), so the button is
  never a trap.

  Both card lists are rendered by `webpack/volunteer/opportunities.ts` from ONE
  markup builder (`memberCardHtml`), so the two sections read as one page rather
  than two features. The "nothing open" card below is the static third instance of
  that same shape — when the builder changes, change this block with it.

  Every id below is one `webpack/volunteer/opportunities.ts` looks for: the bundle
  did not change when the page moved (P15), so none of them may be renamed here.
  What DID change is the markup inside them — `#opportunities-empty` is no longer a
  Tabler `.empty` block but a card in the availability list, carrying the page's only
  **Back to my schedule** button.

  An empty list is a **first-class state, not an error** (§5.6): a card saying
  nothing is open right now, never a spinner that never resolves.
#}

{% block content %}
<div class="portal-volunteer">

    {% include 'volunteer/partials/tabs.html.twig' %}

    <div id="volunteer-opportunities">

        {#
          Ministries looking for help (D19, design §5.6).

          ABOVE the shift list on purpose: a volunteer with no qualifications yet
          sees an empty shift list, and this is the section that gives them
          somewhere to go. The whole block is hidden by opportunities.ts when no
          ministry is advertising — a heading over nothing is worse than silence.
        #}
        <div class="d-none" id="help-wanted-section">
            <h3 class="h4 mb-2">{{ gettext('Ministries looking for help') }}</h3>
            <p class="text-body-secondary">
                {{ gettext('These ministries would like more people. Tell them you are interested and someone will be in touch.') }}
            </p>
            <div id="help-wanted-content"></div>
            <hr class="my-4">
        </div>

        {#
          Upcoming availability. Unlike the section above, this heading pair is
          ALWAYS shown: "nothing is open" is an answer to the question the page
          asks, and a member who came here to look for a slot deserves to be told
          that in words rather than to find the page apparently missing a section.
        #}
        <h3 class="h4 mb-2">{{ gettext('Upcoming availability') }}</h3>
        <p class="text-body-secondary">
            {{ gettext('These scheduled positions still need someone.') }}
        </p>

        <div class="volunteer-loading text-center py-4" id="opportunities-loading">
            <span class="spinner-border spinner-border-sm text-secondary me-2" role="status" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            {{ gettext('Loading') }}
        </div>

        <div class="alert alert-danger d-none" role="alert" id="opportunities-error">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <span class="volunteer-error-text"></span>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-danger ms-2" id="opportunities-retry">{{ gettext('Retry') }}</button>
        </div>

        <div class="d-none" id="opportunities-empty">
            <div class="card mb-3 volunteer-nothing-open-card">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2 justify-content-between align-items-start">
                        <div>
                            <div class="volunteer-card-title volunteer-nothing-open-title fw-bold">
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-calendar-check me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ gettext('Nothing open right now') }}
                            </div>
                            <p class="volunteer-card-text text-body-secondary mt-2 mb-0">
                                {{ gettext('We will email you when something needs filling.') }}
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="mt-3 d-grid gap-2 d-sm-flex volunteer-card-actions">
                        <a class="btn btn-primary volunteer-touch-target" href="{{ url('/portal/volunteer/schedule') }}">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-calendar-check me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ gettext('Back to my schedule') }}
                        </a>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="d-none" id="opportunities-content"></div>
    </div>

</div>
{% endblock %}

{% block scripts_extra %}
<script nonce="{{ nonce() }}" src="{{ asset('/skin/v2/volunteer-opportunities.min.js') }}"></script>
{% endblock %}
